<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · city</p><h1 class="enc-title">Kastamonu</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Kastamonu is a city in northern <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/turkey">Turkey</a>, capital of Kastamonu Province, in the hills south of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/black-sea">Black Sea</a> coast. Held by the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/byzantine-empire">Byzantines</a> under the Komnenoi, it fell to Turkish rulers in the 12th and 13th centuries and became the seat of the Chobanids and, from 1309, of the Candarid <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/beylik">beylik</a> until the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ottoman-empire">Ottomans</a> annexed it in 1461. Its castle and many mosques survive from these periods.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/kastamonu.jpg" alt="Kastamonu" width="320" height="214" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Bertramz · CC BY-SA 3.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Kastamonu1.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
